      "entry_id": "sqli-error-quote",
      "technique": "error-based",
      "text": "{\"detection_method\": \"Vary one injection parameter while holding other inputs constant. Compare the normal response and candidate response for a new database-specific error, including errors present in HTML source.\", \"functional_semantics\": \"A quote can change the boundary of a SQL literal and cause the database parser to return a syntax error through the HTTP response.\", \"limitations\": \"A generic HTTP 500 is not a database-specific error. The probe is diagnostic evidence, not proof that data extraction succeeded; a filtered quote can produce no signal.\", \"title\": \"Quote-induced SQL syntax error\", \"vulnerability_type\": \"error-based\"}",
      "text_sha256": "02a4b827b093139e90b52e4c429fccc5c9d422d4a32e6c8bedc7198e59635efe",
      "source_refs": [
