      "entry_id": "sqli-error-xml",
      "technique": "error-based",
      "text": "{\"detection_method\": \"Compare with the normal response and look for the chosen marker inside the XML/XPath database error. A missing-function error must be distinguished from the intended marker-bearing diagnostic.\", \"functional_semantics\": \"An invalid XPath argument to EXTRACTVALUE or UPDATEXML can deliberately raise a database error containing a chosen marker if the function is available.\", \"limitations\": \"Function availability varies across MySQL/MariaDB versions. The payload is a syntax template requiring context adaptation, not a verified result for a particular target.\", \"title\": \"MySQL-compatible deliberate XML error\", \"vulnerability_type\": \"error-based\"}",
      "text_sha256": "21e0cf60dd1276a41b605d7c850f13f2f1d5756748733571098372fc0e3f771c",
