      "entry_id": "sqli-boolean-template",
      "technique": "boolean-based blind",
      "text": "{\"detection_method\": \"First compare repeated equivalent requests. If dynamic fragments differ, compare a consistent response template. Then compare a matched true/false predicate pair on that template.\", \"functional_semantics\": \"A character comparison can act as a Boolean predicate. Its result is inferred from stable portions of the response when raw pages contain changing content.\", \"limitations\": \"A content-length difference alone is insufficient when pages vary. Filtering must be applied consistently to both controls without removing the meaningful signal.\", \"title\": \"Stable response comparison for Boolean inference\", \"vulnerability_type\": \"boolean-based blind\"}",
      "text_sha256": "0e736273abcdce676306143831b55afaa9ef284183a2689dd73396f045269bc6",
