      "entry_id": "sqli-time-conditional",
      "technique": "time-based blind",
      "text": "{\"detection_method\": \"Measure the candidate against a structurally matched no-delay control using the same injection point. Change the predicate while retaining the delay duration and request structure.\", \"functional_semantics\": \"IF evaluates a predicate and calls SLEEP only on the chosen branch. The induced delay supplies a timing signal when content and SQL errors reveal little.\", \"limitations\": \"SQL context, engine function support and predicate evaluation affect whether SLEEP executes. Latency alone does not prove a conditional SQL delay.\", \"title\": \"Conditional SQL sleep in a numeric input\", \"vulnerability_type\": \"time-based blind\"}",
      "text_sha256": "cc0aa1420c410011fd391dbcf35fc1c50d34e26763c4b967e21c55ebd38ad4b5",
      "source_refs": [
